d daily alcohol consumption (5 drinks/day)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Chronic Liver Disease from Alcohol Use: less likely due to acute presentation pattern", "Exercise-Induced Hepatic Ischemia: uncommon without prior liver dysfunction history", "Gastrointestinal Obstruction from Rapid Weight Loss: possible but lacks direct evidence (e.g., distension, bowel sounds)"], "alarm_features": ["Hemodynamic instability (shock)", "Uncharacterised β-hCG result"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Acute Gynecological Emergency with Hemodynamic Instability", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.44814033587594315, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["β-hCG pending and unprotected sex provide weak support for gynecological causes like ruptured ectopic pregnancy, though absence of typical symptoms like amenor…"], "evidence_against": ["Lack of typical gynecological symptoms moderately reduces the likelihood of a primary gynecological emergency despite β-hCG pending."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Acute Biliary Tract Obstruction with Hemodynamic Instability", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.3734502798966194, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The combination of RUQ pain, alcohol use, and weight loss weakly supports biliary obstruction but lacks specificity for common bile duct stones."], "evidence_against": ["Missing biliary signs like jaundice and elevated bilirubin moderately reduces suspicion for common bile duct stones."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2"